    @tableofcontents

    @section grpcintro grpc Module Introduction

    The \c grpc module provides gRPC client/server and protobuf support for %Qore using dynamic
    protobuf schema loading — users load \c .proto files at runtime and work with %Qore hashes,
    with no code generation required.

    The module is built natively on %Qore's HTTP/2 infrastructure, not wrapping libgrpc++. The
    native Arrow bindings use the distribution's \c libarrow library. Protobuf schema
    support comes from Qore's built-in \c protobuf module.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires grpc" in your code for native Arrow support and
    \c "%requires GrpcUtil" for the gRPC protocol layer.

